  "_design": "Three shelves rising north, each closed by a rock band with one notch to climb and two ledges to come down. The notches are deliberately far apart, so the road zigzags to find them. The stone at 23,7 stays shut until Kellowmere -- at the top of this route -- hands over Shoulder.",
  "_plan": "The climb to Kellowmere, in shelves. Each shelf is a cliff with exactly one way up, and the ways up are deliberately not above one another. The ledges are the way back down and only work that way. The stone heaps are quarry spoil, stepped rather than square, because nothing tipped out of a cart lands in a rectangle."
